{"updated_at": {"date": {"d": "16", "m": "11", "Y": "2026"}, "time": {"H": "03", "M": "35", "S": "58"}}, "news": [{"title": "New World Development's shares tumble after $3.2 billion rights plan", "para": "Shares of New World Development plummeted over 30% following the announcement of a major rights issue. The company plans to offer 11 rights shares at a steep discount from its previous closing price. This decision aims to tackle its significant debt burden and enhance liquidity, with core shareholder Chow Tai Fook Enterprises fully supporting the initiative.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/international/new-world-developments-shares-tumble-after-3-2-billion-rights-plan/135871314?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-178862/135871314.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "international"}, {"title": "China's new home prices fall 2.4% in October; slowest annual decline in almost a year", "para": "In October, home prices in China fell by 0.1%, mirroring September's decline, while the annual decrease moderated to 2.4%, marking the slowest drop since November 2025. Shanghai stood out with rising prices in both new and resale markets. Struggling property investments and sales negatively impacted local economies, prompting the government to introduce measures aimed at stabilizing prices and boosting consumer spending.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/international/chinas-new-home-prices-fall-2-4-in-october-slowest-annual-decline-in-almost-a-year/135871167?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-91812/135871195.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "international"}, {"title": "Homebuyers' body FPCE seeks national appellate tribunal for real estate, similar to NCLAT, NGT", "para": "The Forum for People's Collective Efforts (FPCE) has called for enhanced accountability from state real estate regulatory authorities under the RERA framework. They advocate for a national appellate tribunal dedicated to safeguarding consumer rights nationwide. Additionally, the FPCE proposed several amendments, including a full refund policy for clients in distress.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/residential/homebuyers-body-fpce-seeks-national-appellate-tribunal-for-real-estate-similar-to-nclat-ngt/135871016?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-180784/135871091.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "residential"}]}